From: Nuno Felicio <nuno.felicio@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 04 Aug 2026 01:09:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ports/linux: return ENOSYS for openat2 in syscall() wrapper

Ubuntu updated tar on 22.04 with the fix for CVE-2025-45582 and now tar
uses the raw openat2 syscall to go inside the directories. pseudo cannot
see this syscall (no glibc wrapper exist), it lose track of the dirfd
and do_package fails with 'tar: Cannot mkdir: Bad address'.

Return ENOSYS for SYS_openat2 like is already done for SYS_renameat2,
this way tar falls back to the normal openat() that pseudo can track.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/ports/linux/pseudo_wrappers.c b/ports/linux/pseudo_wrappers.c
index 7659897..b07e0cb 100644
--- a/ports/linux/pseudo_wrappers.c
+++ b/ports/linux/pseudo_wrappers.c
@@ -78,6 +78,18 @@ syscall(long number, ...) {
 	(void) number;
 #endif
 
+#ifdef SYS_openat2
+	/* openat2 has no glibc wrapper and returns fds pseudo cannot
+	 * track, breaking later *at() calls through them. Return ENOSYS
+	 * so callers (e.g. tar hardened for CVE-2025-45582) take their
+	 * openat() fallback path, which pseudo wraps normally.
+	 */
+	if (number == SYS_openat2) {
+		errno = ENOSYS;
+		return -1;
+	}
+#endif
+
 #ifdef SYS_seccomp
 	/* pseudo and seccomp are incompatible as pseudo uses different syscalls
 	 * so pretend to enable seccomp but really do nothing */
